On Tue, Jan 20, 2009 at 4:51 PM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:
> whoa, this is a new term for me.  "cmevla"?

"cmevla", cme-vla, cmene zei valsi, name words.  Every word in Lojban
that ends with a consonant is a cmevla.  The only use for cmevla is as
names (though they're not the only words that can be used for names).

mu'o mi'e la selkik <-- ti cmevla


